{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options","id":924374,"title":"110 kith options?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-01T03:23:52-07:00","id":924374,"title":"110 kith options?","content":"Wow! I'm just stating my excitement here. I know there were upwards of 30 kiths in canon already, so I'm thrilled to see that we'll get 110 'kith options' (which, I assume, includes Thallain versions of most of the kiths we've already seen, plus some options for customising kiths). <br /> <br /> Will we get a sneak preview of any new kiths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T03:51:46-07:00","id":924381,"title":"","content":"There are currently 65 kiths in the English books already (16 Kithain, of which the oba are an eshu variant and the river hags a redcap variant, 8 Thallain, 14 Nunnehi, 4 Menehune, 10 Hsien, 7 Adhene, 6 Inanimae.) We're getting 4 more Kithain from the foreign-language books. Add... let's say 10 more Thallain, to ensure there's a Thallain for each Kithain. That makes 79.<br /> <br /> Even at that projected maximum, that's still 31 kiths over.<br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder if we're going to see the changelings of areas the original run didn't really cover - Africa, India, Australia, and South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:17:59-07:00","id":924582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=924381#post924381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are currently 65 kiths in the English books already (16 Kithain, of which the oba are an eshu variant and the river hags a redcap variant, 8 Thallain, 14 Nunnehi, 4 Menehune, 10 Hsien, 7 Adhene, 6 Inanimae.) We're getting 4 more Kithain from the foreign-language books. Add... let's say 10 more Thallain, to ensure there's a Thallain for each Kithain. That makes 79.<br /> <br /> Even at that projected maximum, that's still 31 kiths over.<br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder if we're going to see the changelings of areas the original run didn't really cover - Africa, India, Australia, and South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rather a lot, isn't it? Although 'kith options', rather than just 'kiths', suggests to me that at least some of these kiths will be variants of the existing kiths. For example, autumn and Arcadian sidhe, and localised offshoots of the major kiths (I'd like to see, say, Caribbean variants of the eshu, for example). And I wonder if there were ever Middle Eastern kiths planned for Keys to the Kingdom that have made it into the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:33:48-07:00","id":924877,"title":"","content":"Kith options is probably a catch all term for things that aren't really kiths like the hsien &quot;kiths&quot; and the kith variants like river hags<br /> <br /> The 110 number is almost entirely stuff from previous books. There a few new ones though. I'm pretty proud of how the European kiths turned out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T14:32:16-07:00","id":925048,"title":"","content":"marin, may we add the 6 Dauntain and the 4 Merfolk (from Blood-Dimmed Tides) to your total, making 89? Also, you're counting one more Thallain than I. My reference is <a href=\"http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm</a>, and I have Beastie, Boggart, Bogie, Goblin, Murdhacha, Ogre, and Spriggan - who'd I miss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11933-jhardhel","name":"Jhardhel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:34:53-07:00","id":925098,"title":"","content":"Would houses Count as &quot;Kith options&quot;? That counts as 13-14 flavours of variant for each kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:51:43-07:00","id":925160,"title":"","content":"Nope, Matt said the houses don't count to the 110!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T23:06:51-07:00","id":925232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhardhel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=925048#post925048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">marin, may we add the 6 Dauntain and the 4 Merfolk (from Blood-Dimmed Tides) to your total, making 89?</div> </div> </div> </div>I counted two Mer from Blood-Dimmed Tides in my original total, one as Kithain, one as Thallain (possibly need to separate them out). Are you counting the three Mer Houses as distinct?<br /> <br /> Didn't count the Dauntain, and have absolutely no idea whether Matt and co are counting them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you're counting one more Thallain than I. My reference is <a href=\"http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm</a>, and I have Beastie, Boggart, Bogie, Goblin, Murdhacha, Ogre, and Spriggan - who'd I miss? </div> </div> </div>The Aithu, the Eshu Thallain from their Kithbook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T23:48:05-07:00","id":925239,"title":"","content":"I'm expecting we will get variants like Riverhags for a lot of the Kiths. Like take a dot from Sidhe Appearance and add it to something plant themed for flower nymph type beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T03:18:39-07:00","id":925289,"title":"","content":"For reference, my original list and sources:<br /> <br /> Kithain:<br /> boggans, eshu, nockers, pooka, redcaps, satyrs, sidhe, sluagh, trolls (corebooks)<br /> selkies (Immortal Eyes: The Toybox)<br /> clurichauns (Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings)<br /> ghille dhu (Isle of the Mighty)<br /> merfolk (Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> piskies (The Fool's Luck)<br /> river hags (Kithbook: Redcap)<br /> oba (Kithbook: Eshu)<br /> <br /> Thallain:<br /> beasties, boggarts, bogies, goblins, ogres (Shadow Court)<br /> murdhuacha (Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> spriggans (The Fool's Luck)<br /> aithu (Kithbook: Eshu)<br /> <br /> Menehune:<br /> ali'i, kahuna, hana, kokua (Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill)<br /> <br /> Nunnehi:<br /> canotili, inuas, kachinas, may-may-gway-shi, nanehi, numuzo'ho, pu'gwis, rock giants, surems, tunghat, water babies, yunwi amai'yine'hi, yunwi tsundi (Players' Guide)<br /> thought-crafters (Kingdom of Willows)<br /> <br /> Hsien:<br /> fu hsi, hanumen, heng po, nyan, tanuki, chu-ih-yu, chu jung, hou-chi, komuko, suijen (Land of Eight Million Dreams)<br /> <br /> Inanimae:<br /> glomes, kubera, mannikins, ondines, parosemes, solimonds (Inanimae)<br /> <br /> Adhene:<br /> acheri, aonides, fir-bholg, fuath, keremet, moirae, naraka (Denizens of the Dreaming)<br /> <br /> Foreign-language books:<br /> korred, morganed (WoD: France)<br /> wichtel, wolpertinger (Gallain in Trolle, Tr\u00e4umer, tiefe W\u00e4lder; Kithain in C20)<br /> <br /> <br /> One I forgot was the Concordian sidhe getting added in C20, who may be based off of the Autumn Scathach in Book of Lost Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Corrected C20's new sidhe type. 07-04-2016, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:34:43-07:00","id":925428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhardhel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=925048#post925048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">marin, may we add the 6 Dauntain and the 4 Merfolk (from Blood-Dimmed Tides) to your total, making 89? Also, you're counting one more Thallain than I. My reference is <a href=\"http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://jhardhel.neocities.org/refkith.htm</a>, and I have Beastie, Boggart, Bogie, Goblin, Murdhacha, Ogre, and Spriggan - who'd I miss?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dauntain don't count towards the total either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:14:23-07:00","id":925486,"title":"","content":"Wow! Do you think we could see a complete (provisional) list at some point? I'm so thirsty for this book and feel there are only a few tiny snippets so far... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:07:39-07:00","id":925928,"title":"","content":"It sounds like old Changeling is getting as expansive in kith numbers as new Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T19:17:40-07:00","id":926212,"title":"","content":"WHat about Kith only Merits? Do they count to the 110?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:34:00-07:00","id":929291,"title":"","content":"Now I'm trying to remember how the hell I got to 110. I'll be honest, math is never my strongest point.<br /> <br /> Lot, it's a lot, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:06:52-07:00","id":998033,"title":"","content":"It's a pity the old CtD-crew never got around to do Nordic kithains (The Troll are in an odd way not at all like Nordic trolls but more of a honorable non-fomorian version of a Hrimthurs (Frostgiant)).<br /> The Huldra/Skogsfru would be a perfect Kith. I once tried to do a sourcebook, but failed along the way:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B39XdgAg0JQiYW94ZWh2Y2RmWEU?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B39XdgAg0JQiYW94ZWh2Y2RmWEU?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B39XdgAg0JQiYW94ZWh2Y2RmWEU?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B39XdgAg0JQiYW94ZWh2Y2RmWEU?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4436-leri","name":"Leri","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T21:21:50-07:00","id":998074,"title":"","content":"Instead of detailing more and even more kiths to be specific to any individual fairy tale they found, it would have been better to make each of the original kiths more archetypal. Pooka should have been for any faerie that was an animal - not just tricksters. That would have covered any number of animal brides, talking animals, and others. &quot;Satyrs&quot; should have been any creature which combined parts of human and animals - not just satyrs, but centaurs, mermaids, harpies and so on. Leprechauns are simply Irish cobblers - so they are boggans. No need for their own kith. And any non-European faeries/invisible people/little people should follow the same kiths for the same reason.<br /> <br /> That they needed to create however many hundred plus kiths is just an indication of poor design to begin with. It's too bad because it didn't need to be that way. They were very close to achieving the elegance of the rest of the game line. There was some room for expansion, but they could probably cover almost any archetype with about twelve kiths at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:47:11-07:00","id":998118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=998074#post998074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of detailing more and even more kiths to be specific to any individual fairy tale they found, it would have been better to make each of the original kiths more archetypal. Pooka should have been for any faerie that was an animal - not just tricksters. That would have covered any number of animal brides, talking animals, and others. &quot;Satyrs&quot; should have been any creature which combined parts of human and animals - not just satyrs, but centaurs, mermaids, harpies and so on. Leprechauns are simply Irish cobblers - so they are boggans. No need for their own kith. And any non-European faeries/invisible people/little people should follow the same kiths for the same reason.<br /> <br /> That they needed to create however many hundred plus kiths is just an indication of poor design to begin with. It's too bad because it didn't need to be that way. They were very close to achieving the elegance of the rest of the game line. There was some room for expansion, but they could probably cover almost any archetype with about twelve kiths at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>They appear to have realised this themselves, as they went with something similar to that proposal for Changeling: The Lost (Seeming as archetype, Kith as more specific example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:14:40-07:00","id":998771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=998074#post998074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of detailing more and even more kiths to be specific to any individual fairy tale they found, it would have been better to make each of the original kiths more archetypal. Pooka should have been for any faerie that was an animal - not just tricksters. That would have covered any number of animal brides, talking animals, and others. &amp;quot;Satyrs&amp;quot; should have been any creature which combined parts of human and animals - not just satyrs, but centaurs, mermaids, harpies and so on. Leprechauns are simply Irish cobblers - so they are boggans. No need for their own kith. And any non-European faeries/invisible people/little people should follow the same kiths for the same reason.<br /> <br /> That they needed to create however many hundred plus kiths is just an indication of poor design to begin with. It's too bad because it didn't need to be that way. They were very close to achieving the elegance of the rest of the game line. There was some room for expansion, but they could probably cover almost any archetype with about twelve kiths at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but part of Changeling's appeal was the vast number of kiths. It's irrational but so are people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:04:12-07:00","id":1073725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=925289#post925289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, my original list and sources:<br /> <br /> Kithain:<br /> boggans, eshu, nockers, pooka, redcaps, satyrs, sidhe, sluagh, trolls (corebooks)<br /> selkies (Immortal Eyes: The Toybox)<br /> clurichauns (Immortal Eyes: Court of All Kings)<br /> ghille dhu (Isle of the Mighty)<br /> merfolk (Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> piskies (The Fool's Luck)<br /> river hags (Kithbook: Redcap)<br /> oba (Kithbook: Eshu)<br /> <br /> Thallain:<br /> beasties, boggarts, bogies, goblins, ogres (Shadow Court)<br /> murdhuacha (Blood-Dimmed Tides)<br /> spriggans (The Fool's Luck)<br /> aithu (Kithbook: Eshu)<br /> <br /> Menehune:<br /> ali'i, kahuna, hana, kokua (Immortal Eyes: Shadows on the Hill)<br /> <br /> Nunnehi:<br /> canotili, inuas, kachinas, may-may-gway-shi, nanehi, numuzo'ho, pu'gwis, rock giants, surems, tunghat, water babies, yunwi amai'yine'hi, yunwi tsundi (Players' Guide)<br /> thought-crafters (Kingdom of Willows)<br /> <br /> Hsien:<br /> fu hsi, hanumen, heng po, nyan, tanuki, chu-ih-yu, chu jung, hou-chi, komuko, suijen (Land of Eight Million Dreams)<br /> <br /> Inanimae:<br /> glomes, kubera, mannikins, ondines, parosemes, solimonds (Inanimae)<br /> <br /> Adhene:<br /> acheri, aonides, fir-bholg, fuath, keremet, moirae, naraka (Denizens of the Dreaming)<br /> <br /> Foreign-language books:<br /> korred, morganed (WoD: France)<br /> wichtel, wolpertinger (Gallain in Trolle, Tr\u00e4umer, tiefe W\u00e4lder; Kithain in C20)<br /> <br /> <br /> One I forgot was the Concordian sidhe getting added in C20, who may be based off of the Autumn Scathach in Book of Lost Houses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hey guys. Does anyone have the illustrations from the book Trolle, Tr\u00e4umer, tiefe W\u00e4lder? I wanted the official illustrations of Gallain wichtel and wolpertinger.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9100-morlockiller","name":"Morlockiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:19:42-07:00","id":1073755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morlockiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/924374-110-kith-options?p=1073725#post1073725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. Does anyone have the illustrations from the book Trolle, Tr\u00e4umer, tiefe W\u00e4lder? I wanted the official illustrations of Gallain wichtel and wolpertinger.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, funny thing about the wichtel and the wolpertinger we discovered while creating that stretch goal. The section heading for them in Trolle, Traumer, tiefe Walder is Gallain. Their actual write-ups in the German book treat them more like chimera. The wichtel, if you squint and look at them funny could maybe be construed as a type of fae but not given any rules with which to make a player character. The wolpertinger, though, are straight up chimera in the German book.<br /> <br /> They're full on playable Kithain kiths in C20 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a copy of the book, but I don't have a scan of their illustrations. If I get a chance after I'm home from work, I'll see if I can take a picture of them. I don't expect their illustrations in C20 will look exactly like they look in the German book \u2014 especially the wolpertinger since they'll be changelings in human bodies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T16:14:47-07:00","id":1073918,"title":"","content":"Here is the wichtel:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shad